    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Core Curriculum Directive:</strong> Every 4-act narrative block across the platform must be anchored by an authentic, academically verified primary source plate (1 source per block target). Visual sources are never decorative; each plate must drive disciplinary historical inquiry with complete provenance, context, targeted hinge questions, and dual-perspective discussion prompts.
    </div>

    <h2>The 4-Layer Human &amp; Multimodal Verification Protocol</h2>
    <p>To prevent fake imagery, modern cinematic stills (e.g. <em>Bridge of Spies</em>), living-history reenactors, or mislabeled internet reposts from compromising the curriculum, every visual asset must pass four strict gates:</p>

    <div class="protocol-grid">
      <div class="protocol-card p1">
        <div class="protocol-title">
          <span>Layer 1: Code &amp; File Pre-Flight</span>
          <span class="phase-badge">Automated</span>
        </div>
        <p>Scripts (<code>audit_and_verify_sources_visually.cjs</code>) verify physical existence on disk (&gt;0 bytes), exact image dimensions, zero 404 network errors, and complete schema integrity. Medium-mismatch guards flag mismatched types (e.g. portraits mapped to maps).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="protocol-card p2">
        <div class="protocol-title">
          <span>Layer 2: Archival Provenance</span>
          <span class="phase-badge">Academic Rights</span>
        </div>
        <p>Every asset is registered in <code>master_rights_database.json</code> with official accession numbers and permanent catalog URLs from accredited repositories: Imperial War Museums (IWM), US National Archives (NARA), Library of Congress (LOC), UK National Archives (Kew), and Bundesarchiv.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="protocol-card p3">
        <div class="protocol-title">
          <span>Layer 3: Multimodal Vision Inspection</span>
          <span class="phase-badge">Multi-Modal AI / Human</span>
        </div>
        <p>Direct pixel analysis (via <code>view_file</code>) of the binary file. Verifies authentic period grain, genuine documentary context, and absence of modern film actors, CGI elements, watermark crops, or anachronistic details.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="protocol-card p4">
        <div class="protocol-title">
          <span>Layer 4: In-App Render &amp; Sign-Off Gate</span>
          <span class="phase-badge">Production Preview</span>
        </div>
        <p>Browser-based inspection in the live lesson drawer and <code>source_visual_verification_gallery.html</code>. Validates aspect ratio, legible captions, archival citation line, targeted hinge question, and model exam discussion ideas.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

