    <h2>Mandatory Pedagogical Source Schema &amp; Disciplinary Standards</h2>
    <p>Every source object registered in a unit's <code>data.js</code> must implement the rigorous five-fold pedagogical schema:</p>
    
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; font-size: 7.5pt;">
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px;">
        <strong style="color: #0284c7;">1. Archival Metadata &amp; Citation:</strong>
        <p style="margin: 2px 0 0 0; color: #475569;">Descriptive Title (<code>Source A: Creator, Title (Date)</code>), clean image path in <code>/images/</code>, archival citation line referencing holding repository and accession ID.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px;">
        <strong style="color: #059669;">2. Context &amp; Mandatory Hinge Question:</strong>
        <p style="margin: 2px 0 0 0; color: #475569;">Succinct historical contextualisation (2–3 sentences) concluding with a targeted hinge question compelling pupils to interrogate purpose, perspective, or reliability.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px;">
        <strong style="color: #d97706;">3. Provenance Clues (Tripartite Analysis):</strong>
        <p style="margin: 2px 0 0 0; color: #475569;">Three explicit analytical bullet points dissecting: (a) <strong>Author/Creator</strong> status, (b) Intended <strong>Audience</strong>, and (c) Underlying ideological or political <strong>Motive</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px;">
        <strong style="color: #7c3aed;">4. Dual-Perspective Discussion Ideas:</strong>
        <p style="margin: 2px 0 0 0; color: #475569;">At least two balanced model interpretive angles for classroom teacher facilitation and high-mark utility analysis in exams (value vs limitation).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-footer">
      <div>The History Revision Hub • Independent Curriculum Architecture</div>
      <div>Master Visual Source Curriculum Roadmap • Page 2 of 2</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
`;

async function generatePdf() {
  console.log('🚀 Launching Puppeteer to compile Master Visual Source Curriculum Roadmap PDF...');
  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({
    headless: 'new',
    executablePath: 'C:\\Program Files\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\chrome.exe',
    args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-setuid-sandbox', '--disable-web-security']
  });

  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.setContent(htmlContent, { waitUntil: 'networkidle0' });
  await page.evaluateHandle('document.fonts.ready');

  // Render to Desktop
  console.log(`🖨️ Rendering Master Roadmap PDF to Desktop: ${desktopPath}`);
  await page.pdf({
    path: desktopPath,
    format: 'A4',
    printBackground: true,
    margin: {
      top: '0mm',
      bottom: '0mm',
      left: '0mm',
      right: '0mm'
    }
  });

  // Render to Public PDFs
  console.log(`🖨️ Rendering backup copy to Public PDFs: ${publicPdfPath}`);
  await page.pdf({
    path: publicPdfPath,
    format: 'A4',
    printBackground: true,
    margin: {
      top: '0mm',
      bottom: '0mm',
      left: '0mm',
      right: '0mm'
    }
  });

  await browser.close();
  console.log('🎉 Successfully compiled Master Visual Source Roadmap PDF to Desktop and Public PDFs!');
}

generatePdf().catch(err => {
  console.error('❌ Failed to generate Roadmap PDF:', err);
  process.exit(1);
});
